<theodulf. carm. 49.1>	Martyr amoene, tuos hic Christus condidit artus,
<theodulf. carm. 49.2>	Et tua mens centri scandit ad alta volans.
<theodulf. carm. 49.3>	Tu Tiberina tuis lustrasti littora gestis,
<theodulf. carm. 49.4>	Et nunc Rhenicolas ossis honore beas.
<theodulf. carm. 49.5>	Roma, favente deo vidisti in martyre signa,
<theodulf. carm. 49.6>	Nunc, Germana cohors, cernis id ipsud opus.
<theodulf. carm. 49.7>	Aulica silvestri delubra in rure locasti,
<theodulf. carm. 49.8>	Martyr, et in vacuis syrtibus aula micat.
<theodulf. carm. 49.9>	Nazarium vocitat hunc florem natio cuncta,
<theodulf. carm. 49.10>	Nam nazar Hebraea flos bene lingua vocat.
<theodulf. carm. 49.11>	Hunc ego Wangionum veniens festinus ab urbe
<theodulf. carm. 49.12>	Dum peterem, vidi nube nivem cadere.
<theodulf. carm. 49.13>	Pisciflui Rheni transivi in robore ripas,
<theodulf. carm. 49.14>	Ut citius possem eius adire locum.
